# ── Secrets / environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API keys (Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter, Anthropic, OpenAI), local overrides.
# .env.* alone would also hide *.env.example — carve that back out explicitly
# so example/template env files stay versioned.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.local
.env.production

# ── Application data (100% local, personal) ─────────────────────────────────
# Everything under cortex-server/data/ : SQLite DB, LanceDB vectors, uploaded
# images, backups, watched inbox, imported corpus, uploaded/processed files,
# temp audio/video from transcription — all personal, never versioned.
cortex-server/data/

# ── Test scratch DBs (recreated from scratch by the tests themselves via
# fs.rmSync + initSqlite on every run — never meant to hold real content) ───
cortex-server/data-test-*/
# Same test-scratch pattern can also land at the repo root depending on a
# test file's relative cwd (e.g. run from outside cortex-server/) — one
# such root-level dir/test.db was found already committed by accident
# before this rule existed; see the git-tracked-file note in the audit.
data-test-*/

# ── TLS certificates (mobile/HTTPS dev mode) ─────────────────────────────────
certs/

# ── Private key / TLS material and SQLite files anywhere ─────────────────────
# RASSILON_LAN_TLS_KEY_PATH / RASSILON_LAN_TLS_CERT_PATH and SQLITE_PATH can
# point outside certs/ and cortex-server/data/; no such file is tracked.
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
cortex-server/bin/*.exe
cortex-server/node_modules/
docteur-voice/node_modules/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
.vite/
coverage/

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/

# ── Temp / cache ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmp/
temp/
.tmp/
.cache/
*.tmp
*.pid
*.lock

# ── Ad hoc E2E/manual-QA artifacts (neurons, agents, scripts created and
# cleaned up during a testing pass are prefixed this way — guards against one
# being committed by accident if cleanup is missed) ──────────────────────────
__E2E_TEST__*

# ── MetaGPT V1 runtime artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python bytecode cache from the MetaGPT policy/runner modules under
# cortex-server/src/lib/ (no existing Python rule in this repo otherwise).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# metagpt_runner_apply.py's atomic write uses a same-directory temp file
# (.{name}.mg6-tmp-{pid}) before os.replace(); normally renamed away or
# deleted on failure, but guards against one surviving a crash mid-write.
.mg6-tmp-*
# MG-5B/MG-6J sample outputs applied under src/ after an approved diff —
# disposable demo/smoke content, never part of the real application source.
src/_metagpt_generated_samples/

# Python tool caches — no existing rule covered these (only bytecode was
# handled above); MetaGPT/local tooling can generate them during test runs.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Python virtualenvs — not currently committed, but no existing rule guarded
# against one being created locally under either common name.
.venv/
venv/

# ── Studio browser-test evidence (Playwright screenshots, regenerated by
# scripts/test-*-studio-browser.mjs on every run — never committed by any
# existing Studio either) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
reports/studios-evidence/

# Playwright's own default report/result output dirs (distinct from the
# repo's own reports/studios-evidence/ above) — not currently produced by
# any script here, but the default Playwright config would write to these.
playwright-report/
test-results/

# ── OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
Desktop.ini
*.temp

# ── IDE / editor project settings (local machine, not shared; nothing under
# either dir is currently tracked) ──────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Claude Code project settings (local machine, not shared) ───────────────
.claude/

# Sherlock dedicated environment: dependencies and temporary setup HOME.
external/Sherlock-runtime/
/external/MetaGPT/
/external/OpenMontage/
